Description: Qt6 native GUI for GRASS GIS
 qtgrass is a full-featured Qt6 graphical user interface for GRASS GIS,
 replacing the legacy wxPython interface with a native C++/Qt6 application.
 .
 Features include:
  - Map canvas with raster/vector rendering and layer management
  - Module dialog launcher for all GRASS modules
  - Graphical modeler (.gxm) with node-graph editor
  - Vector digitizer with undo/redo (v.edit)
  - Temporal animation player (STRDS/STVDS) with MP4 export
  - Print composer with PDF/PNG/SVG export
  - Database manager with SQL editor and field calculator
  - Supervised classification (iclass) with scatter plots
  - Georectification with GCP table and RMS computation
  - 3-D terrain view via OpenGL 3.3 heightmap renderer
  - WMS/WMTS browser, map swipe comparison, network analysis launcher
  - Time-series plot (tplot) and map history browser
 .
 GRASS GIS 8.0 or later must be installed separately.  Build against a
 local GRASS installation by passing -DGRASS_PREFIX=/path to cmake.
